371	1039,407,1637,850	371. Passion-Flower No. 1, enlarged.	An open Passion-Flower seen from the side: narrow spreading sepals and petals, the fringed crown round the centre, and the stalked ovary rising with its anthers and three large-headed styles.
372	831,1170,1071,1483	Garden Gooseberry: 372. with flowers;	A piece of gooseberry stem with a cluster of small five-parted flowers and a young leaf above a spreading set of three long thorns.
373	35,1147,1143,1955 - 820,1130,1085,1485 - 100,1745,616,1995 - 700,1838,958,1995	373. with fruit.	A fruiting gooseberry branch with lobed, toothed leaves, thorns at the joints, and round bristly berries hanging singly beneath.
374	708,1838,953,1966	374. Cup of the calyx laid open, bearing the 5 little petals and stamens.	The calyx-cup slit and spread flat, its rim bearing the small petals alternating with the stamens.
375	552,1777,616,1973	375. The pistil.	The pistil: a small bristly ovary below, a tuft of hairs, and a slender style forked at the top.
376	320,1748,496,1975	376. Young berry cut across.	A young bristly berry cut across, showing the flat seeds packed in the pulp of the single cell.
377	110,1751,309,1975	377. Young berry divided lengthwise.	A young bristly berry split lengthwise, the seeds lying along its walls and the withered remains of the flower at one end and the stalk at the other.
